WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.275
The decision belongs to a few people.

2
00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:07.900
The executive sponsor, with the CIO,
owns scope, funding and sequence.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.425
The steward owns the target
design and the early gates.

4
00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:14.588
And workstream leads say
when their area is ready.

5
00:00:14.588 --> 00:00:18.864
To make the conversation concrete,
bring four local numbers:

6
00:00:18.864 --> 00:00:24.679
how many Windows Server 2019 servers you
run, how many contractors sit outside the

7
00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:28.955
HR system, how long it takes a
departing person to lose access,

8
00:00:28.955 --> 00:00:30.238
and your HR 2.0 wave.

9
00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:34.217
Then ask for one decision:
approve the four-week pre-flight,

10
00:00:34.217 --> 00:00:36.538
with a named owner and a start date.

11
00:00:36.538 --> 00:00:39.373
Episode 4, Making the Case at Your Agency,

12
00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:42.600
turns this into a one-page
ask for the meeting.
